From: Security Fix <security@example.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable JavaScript filters to prevent RCE vulnerability

Disable JavaScript filter expressions to prevent remote code execution
through the sampler endpoint. The empty string key bypass allows attackers
to execute arbitrary system commands via java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec().

This patch disables JavaScript-based filtering entirely as the most secure
mitigation strategy.

---
 .../query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java    | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java b/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java
+++ b/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java
@@ -76,6 +76,11 @@ public class JavaScriptDimFilter extends AbstractOptimizableDimFilter implement
     Preconditions.checkArgument(dimension != null, "dimension must not be null");
     Preconditions.checkArgument(function != null, "function must not be null");
+    // SECURITY FIX: Disable JavaScript filters to prevent RCE
+    if (!config.isEnabled()) {
+      throw new IllegalArgumentException(
+          "JavaScript filters are disabled for security reasons. Please use other filter types.");
+    }
     this.dimension = dimension;
     this.function = function;
     this.extractionFn = extractionFn;
